1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:02,235
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:02,299 --> 00:00:06,829
Basil tests which makes a stronger electromagnet, an iron nail or a

3
00:00:06,849 --> 00:00:07,849
steel nail.

4
00:00:08,139 --> 00:00:12,309
He coils twenty-five turns round the iron nail, but only eight turns

5
00:00:12,329 --> 00:00:13,499
round the steel nail.

6
00:00:13,789 --> 00:00:14,979
Is his test fair?

7
00:00:15,117 --> 00:00:16,227
One, yes.

8
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:18,377
Two, no.

9
00:00:19,855 --> 00:00:21,365
Hold on to your answer!

10
00:00:23,587 --> 00:00:25,767
Our mini crane needs the strongest hook.

11
00:00:25,947 --> 00:00:28,717
So I am testing an iron nail and a steel nail!

12
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:31,760
A little woodlouse is hiding in this video.

13
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:33,250
Can you spot it?

14
00:00:33,606 --> 00:00:35,996
Woodlice love dark, damp corners.

15
00:00:36,156 --> 00:00:37,226
Look low!

16
00:00:37,499 --> 00:00:38,959
You against the Buddies!

17
00:00:39,229 --> 00:00:41,079
Lock in first with your fingers.

18
00:00:41,349 --> 00:00:43,179
One finger for every point.

19
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:45,135
Today you'll learn:

20
00:00:45,337 --> 00:00:47,017
What an experiment does.

21
00:00:47,295 --> 00:00:48,835
What a fair test is.

22
00:00:49,109 --> 00:00:50,979
How to spot an unfair test.

23
00:00:51,476 --> 00:00:52,416
Are you ready?

24
00:00:52,856 --> 00:00:53,626
Three!

25
00:00:54,006 --> 00:00:54,666
Two!

26
00:00:55,036 --> 00:00:55,686
One!

27
00:00:56,106 --> 00:00:56,826
Go!

28
00:00:58,315 --> 00:00:59,205
Round one!

29
00:00:59,515 --> 00:01:01,065
Is Basil's test fair?

30
00:01:01,355 --> 00:01:02,445
One, yes.

31
00:01:02,725 --> 00:01:03,565
Two, no.

32
00:01:03,865 --> 00:01:05,175
Show me your fingers!

33
00:01:10,691 --> 00:01:11,671
Locked in!

34
00:01:11,949 --> 00:01:12,559
One!

35
00:01:12,709 --> 00:01:15,909
It's my test, and my iron nail picked up the most clips.

36
00:01:16,089 --> 00:01:17,179
Iron wins!

37
00:01:17,528 --> 00:01:21,318
Two. The iron nail has many more turns of wire.

38
00:01:21,618 --> 00:01:23,308
Maybe the turns did it.

39
00:01:23,657 --> 00:01:24,427
Two.

40
00:01:24,897 --> 00:01:27,737
Basil changed the nail, and he changed the turns too.

41
00:01:28,387 --> 00:01:29,907
Be a steel paper clip!

42
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:31,167
Shrink down.

43
00:01:31,447 --> 00:01:32,377
Quietly.

44
00:01:34,660 --> 00:01:37,560
You are a steel paper clip, lying in a tray.

45
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:42,440
Above you hangs Basil's iron nail, wrapped in many, many turns of

46
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:43,160
wire.

47
00:01:43,745 --> 00:01:45,215
It pulls you up, hard!

48
00:01:46,045 --> 00:01:48,955
You cling to its tip with lots of other clips.

49
00:01:49,725 --> 00:01:52,875
Over there, the steel nail has only a few turns.

50
00:01:53,655 --> 00:01:54,995
Its pull is weak.

51
00:01:55,584 --> 00:01:56,604
But you wonder.

52
00:01:57,444 --> 00:01:59,304
Was it the iron that pulled you?

53
00:02:00,074 --> 00:02:01,514
Or all those turns?

54
00:02:02,284 --> 00:02:03,534
You cannot tell!

55
00:02:05,394 --> 00:02:08,484
The answer is two: Basil's test is not fair!

56
00:02:08,724 --> 00:02:10,314
Did you show two fingers?

57
00:02:10,594 --> 00:02:12,004
Put one finger up!

58
00:02:12,354 --> 00:02:15,504
A variable is a thing that can change in a test, such

59
00:02:15,524 --> 00:02:18,214
as the kind of nail, or the number of turns!

60
00:02:18,942 --> 00:02:21,292
But my iron nail picked up the most clips.

61
00:02:21,422 --> 00:02:22,782
Why is that not fair?

62
00:02:23,659 --> 00:02:24,809
Look closer.

63
00:02:25,409 --> 00:02:27,249
Basil changed two things.

64
00:02:27,809 --> 00:02:29,619
The kind of nail is different.

65
00:02:30,209 --> 00:02:32,509
And the number of turns is different too.

66
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:35,170
The iron nail attracts more clips.

67
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:37,540
Was it because of the iron?

68
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:40,360
Or because of the twenty-five turns?

69
00:02:40,930 --> 00:02:42,300
We cannot be sure.

70
00:02:42,649 --> 00:02:45,959
If the experiment is not fair, we will not be sure which

71
00:02:45,979 --> 00:02:48,119
variable can explain the results.

72
00:02:48,755 --> 00:02:51,869
A fair test is a test where we change only one thing,

73
00:02:51,889 --> 00:02:55,383
and keep all the other things the same, such as changing only

74
00:02:55,403 --> 00:02:56,648
the kind of nail!

75
00:03:00,048 --> 00:03:01,348
Say it with me!

76
00:03:02,058 --> 00:03:05,898
To conduct a fair test, scientists need to ensure that only one

77
00:03:05,918 --> 00:03:08,258
thing, called a variable, is changed.

78
00:03:09,058 --> 00:03:11,048
The other variables are kept the same.

79
00:03:13,675 --> 00:03:16,425
Pip, my magnet picked up more pins than yours!

80
00:03:16,485 --> 00:03:18,755
So my magnet is the stronger one!

81
00:03:19,030 --> 00:03:20,590
Something is not right.

82
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:23,040
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

83
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:24,280
Hold on!

84
00:03:29,693 --> 00:03:30,823
Arms crossed?

85
00:03:31,093 --> 00:03:32,303
One finger up!

86
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:35,650
Momo held her magnet close to the pins, and Pip held his

87
00:03:35,670 --> 00:03:36,710
far away.

88
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:38,530
The distance changed too!

89
00:03:38,650 --> 00:03:41,270
Hold them at the same height, over the same pins.

90
00:03:41,550 --> 00:03:43,810
Now only the magnet is different.

91
00:03:43,950 --> 00:03:45,140
That is fair!

92
00:03:45,643 --> 00:03:46,433
Okay!

93
00:03:46,583 --> 00:03:49,033
How do I make my iron and steel test fair?

94
00:03:49,906 --> 00:03:51,056
Look closer.

95
00:03:51,646 --> 00:03:54,136
Give both nails twenty turns of wire.

96
00:03:54,716 --> 00:03:58,146
Use the same kind of battery, the same wire, and the same

97
00:03:58,166 --> 00:03:59,246
steel clips.

98
00:03:59,535 --> 00:04:01,465
Dip both tips the same way.

99
00:04:02,045 --> 00:04:05,295
Now only one thing is different: the kind of nail.

100
00:04:05,875 --> 00:04:09,225
If one nail attracts more clips, we know the nail did it!

101
00:04:09,515 --> 00:04:12,515
An experiment is a test that we plan and do to answer

102
00:04:12,535 --> 00:04:16,895
a question, such as: which nail makes a stronger electromagnet?

103
00:04:20,194 --> 00:04:21,354
Say it with me!

104
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:26,240
When scientists plan and conduct an experiment, they answer a question or

105
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:27,660
test a prediction.

106
00:04:30,214 --> 00:04:31,674
Show me your score hand!

107
00:04:31,954 --> 00:04:32,984
Two fingers?

108
00:04:33,264 --> 00:04:34,634
You beat the Buddies.

109
00:04:34,914 --> 00:04:35,914
High five!

110
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:38,117
Did you spot the woodlouse?

111
00:04:38,407 --> 00:04:40,047
It was under the cupboard door!

112
00:04:40,318 --> 00:04:41,628
Here is a fun fact!

113
00:04:41,698 --> 00:04:44,168
A woodlouse is a cousin of crabs and prawns!

114
00:04:44,288 --> 00:04:46,688
And in a fair test, with a damp side and a dry

115
00:04:46,708 --> 00:04:49,308
side, woodlice crawl to the damp side!

116
00:04:49,513 --> 00:04:50,793
Tell someone at home!

117
00:04:51,522 --> 00:04:53,722
Let's read today's key words together!

118
00:04:54,012 --> 00:04:54,772
Ready?

119
00:04:55,059 --> 00:04:55,929
Variable.

120
00:04:57,389 --> 00:04:58,409
Fair test.

121
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:00,970
Experiment.

122
00:05:02,585 --> 00:05:03,525
Well done!

123
00:05:04,322 --> 00:05:05,322
My turn!

124
00:05:05,442 --> 00:05:09,252
I will test if more batteries make our electromagnet stronger!

125
00:05:09,528 --> 00:05:11,228
Will Momo's plan be fair?

126
00:05:11,518 --> 00:05:13,098
Find out in Part Two!

127
00:05:14,358 --> 00:05:15,459
Say it with us!

128
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:17,010
Ready?

129
00:05:17,133 --> 00:05:17,793
One!

130
00:05:18,133 --> 00:05:18,833
two!

131
00:05:19,138 --> 00:05:20,313
Now you know!
